            "review_title": "Review at Daiichi Ramen & Curry",
            "review_text": "desiremmwekb10\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam2964 contributions\n0\nSo so ramen and curry\nJan 2019 • Solo\nAnother stop in the ramen tour. I ordered tonkotsu shoyu ramen. The broth here is quite different from others. It has a strong flavor of garlic and sesame. It does make a different however it takes away the nice traditional flavor of tonkotsu soup. The ramen is thicker, cooked nice and al dente. The charsiu meat was too lean, a bit dry, and not tender at all. Well, overall, the ramen is not quite up to the standard I'm accustomed to by now. Curry has a nice mild taste and flavor, a bit too sweet though. Fried chicken is dry and not tasty. In term of taste, it's a level behind the previous shops I tried. Just average.\nRead more\nWritten January 4, 2019",
